.TH "LANGUAGEMODEL.PROMPTSTREAMING" "3JS" "August 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
LanguageModel.promptStreaming \- LanguageModel: promptStreaming() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]promptStreaming()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] interface sends input to the language model and
returns a \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] that delivers the model\(cqs
response incrementally as it is generated.
.PP
This is useful for displaying responses to users incrementally for
outputs that take a long time to complete, or for any scenario where
perceived latency should be minimized.
Consume the stream using \f[CR]for await...of\f[R] or by attaching a
reader via \f[CR]ReadableStream.getReader()\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
promptStreaming(input)
promptStreaming(input, options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]input\f[R]
The content to prompt the model with.
This is either:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
A string \(em Shorthand for a single textual message.
.IP \(bu 2
An array of objects, each representing a single message in a
conversation with a language model.
Objects may have the following properties:
.RS 2
.TP
\f[B]role\f[R]
A string indicating the point of view the message is phrased from.
Must be one of:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]system\f[R]
A system\-level instruction that guides the model\(cqs overall behavior.
This must be the first instruction passed to the model.
.TP
\f[B]user\f[R]
A message from the user, which the API should respond to.
.TP
\f[B]assistant\f[R]
An input that provides context for the AI assistant, such as its persona
or the format of its responses.
Such messages mainly serve to provide context/history, and further shape
how the model responds.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]content\f[R]
A string representing a textual prompt, or an array of objects.
Each object includes the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
An enumerated value representing the type of content.
This can be one of:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]audio\f[R]
Audio content.
.TP
\f[B]image\f[R]
Image content.
.TP
\f[B]text\f[R]
Textual content.
.TP
\f[B]tool\-call\f[R]
A tool invocation issued by the model.
.TP
\f[B]tool\-response\f[R]
The result of a tool invocation.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]value\f[R]
The content of the message.
If the \f[CR]type\f[R] is \f[CR]text\f[R], this is always a string.
If the \f[CR]type\f[R] is \f[CR]audio\f[R] or \f[CR]image\f[R], the
\f[CR]value\f[R] can be one of several different object types; see What
data types are accepted?.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]prefix\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A boolean, defaulting to \f[CR]false\f[R].
When \f[CR]true\f[R], the message is treated as a prefix for the
model\(cqs next generated response rather than a complete turn.
.RE
.RE
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
Options for creating a prompt.
Properties include:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]responseConstraint\f[R]
An object following the structure defined by \c
.UR https://json-schema.org/
JSON Schema
.UE \c
\ defining the precise format the model\(cqs output should be delivered
in.
When provided and \f[CR]omitResponseConstraintInput\f[R] is
\f[CR]false\f[R], any implementation\-defined constraint\-description
message is included in the measurement.
.TP
\f[B]omitResponseConstraintInput\f[R]
A boolean; when \f[CR]true\f[R], the automatic constraint\-description
message is excluded from the measurement.
.TP
\f[B]signal\f[R]
An \f[CR]AbortSignal\f[R] to cancel the operation.
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] of \f[CR]String\f[R] chunks.
Each chunk represents a piece of the model\(cqs response as it is
generated.
The stream closes when generation completes.
.SS Exceptions
Errors are surfaced as stream errors rather than as rejected promises.
Consumers should handle errors using a stream\(cqs standard
error\-handling mechanisms.
.TP
\f[B]AbortError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the operation was canceled via the \f[CR]signal\f[R] option.
.TP
\f[B]NotAllowedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if usage of the method is blocked by a \f[CR]language\-model\f[R]
\f[CR]Permissions\-Policy\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]NotSupportedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
A message\(cqs \f[CR]role\f[R] is \f[CR]assistant\f[R] and its
\f[CR]type\f[R] is anything other than \f[CR]text\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
A message\(cqs \f[CR]type\f[R] is \f[CR]text\f[R] and its
\f[CR]value\f[R] is not a string.
.IP \(bu 2
The input or output text is in a language the user agent doesn\(cqt
support for prompting.
.IP \(bu 2
A message\(cqs \f[CR]type\f[R] is \f[CR]image\f[R] or \f[CR]audio\f[R]
but the type was not listed in \f[CR]expectedInputs\f[R], or the
\f[CR]value\f[R] is not an accepted data type.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]OperationError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the prompt fails for any other reason not listed in the other
exception types.
.TP
\f[B]QuotaExceededError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the prompt would cause the session\(cqs context usage to
exceed the model\(cqs \f[CR]LanguageModel.contextWindow\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]SyntaxError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
No messages are included in the messages array.
.IP \(bu 2
A message\(cqs \f[CR]prefix\f[R] property is set to \f[CR]true\f[R] and:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
The message\(cqs \f[CR]role\f[R] is not \f[CR]assistant\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The message is not the last item in the messages array.
.RE
.RE
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]omitResponseConstraintInput\f[R] is \f[CR]true\f[R] but
\f[CR]responseConstraint\f[R] is not provided.
.IP \(bu 2
A message\(cqs \f[CR]role\f[R] is \f[CR]system\f[R] but it was not the
first message passed to the context.
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[CR]promptStreaming()\f[R] method adds the provided input to the
context window and generates a response.
The entire response is receives incrementally as a
\f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R].
.PP
To receive the response as one complete string, use
\f[CR]LanguageModel.prompt()\f[R] instead.
To add content to the context window without generating a response, use
\f[CR]LanguageModel.append()\f[R].
.PP
Each call to \f[CR]promptStreaming()\f[R] adds to the session\(cqs
context.
To branch from a given state without affecting the original session,
call \f[CR]LanguageModel.clone()\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Streaming a response to the page
This example writes out chunks from a \f[CR]promptStreaming()\f[R]
call\(cqs \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] as they arrive.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();
\f[B]const\f[R] output = document.querySelector(\(dq#output\(dq);

\f[B]const\f[R] stream = session.promptStreaming(\(dqWrite a short poem about the ocean.\(dq);

\f[B]for\f[R] \f[B]await\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] chunk \f[B]of\f[R] stream) {
  output.textContent += chunk;
}
.EE
.PP
See also Using the Prompt API > Complete streaming example.
.SS Streaming with an abort signal
This example shows how to use an \f[CR]AbortController\f[R] with
\f[CR]promptStreaming()\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] controller = \f[B]new\f[R] AbortController();
document
  .querySelector(\(dq#stop\(dq)
  .addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] controller.abort());

\f[B]const\f[R] stream = session.promptStreaming(\(dqTell me a long story.\(dq, {
  signal: controller.signal,
});

\f[B]try\f[R] {
  \f[B]for\f[R] \f[B]await\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] chunk \f[B]of\f[R] stream) {
    output.textContent += chunk;
  }
} \f[B]catch\f[R] (err) {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (err.name === \(dqAbortError\(dq) {
    console.log(\(dqStreaming was stopped by the user.\(dq);
  }
}
.EE
.SS Collecting streamed chunks into a single string
In this example, chunks from a \f[CR]ReadableStream\f[R] are collected
before the whole stream is written out.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();
\f[B]const\f[R] stream = session.promptStreaming(\(dqExplain quantum entanglement.\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] chunks = [];

\f[B]for\f[R] \f[B]await\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] chunk \f[B]of\f[R] stream) {
  chunks.push(chunk);
}

\f[B]const\f[R] fullResponse = chunks.join(\(dq\(dq);
console.log(fullResponse);
.EE
